  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Beyond Air’s core commercial activity is gaining momentum, with sequential revenue growth and a transition to gross profitability indicating accelerating hospital adoption. The pipeline is advancing into higher-value areas, as the UNO program in solid tumors prepares to present Phase 1a data at AACR, potentially opening a significant oncology opportunity. Demand appears to be building without any noted macro or competitive friction, supporting the maintained full-year revenue outlook.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a sharp operational pivot—deeply cutting operating expenses while driving commercial scale—demonstrating disciplined cash management. The planned divestiture of the NeuroNOS subsidiary to XTL Biopharmaceuticals introduces a creative, non-dilutive funding path with milestone upside and retained equity. Recent financing extends cash runway well into the coming year, and the maintained guidance signals confidence in the commercial plan. These moves collectively portray a team reshaping the company’s risk profile through strategic portfolio actions and cost vigilance.",
